@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@ A little bit of background:
 From what I gathered, there is a sensor called GEN1. And as soon it hits 52°C the CPU instantly throttles to 400MHz (the minimum frequency) for several seconds until temps have dropped. From what I found out this is part of the hardware protection and is obviously meant to protect the Pc from damage. However the reaction coded into the firmware is a massive over correction and there is a much better way to fix this. In essence we can tell the Surface Laptop to slow down long before it gets to that threshold, which gives us stable and prolonged performance. All of the tests were performed in the balanced profile setting.
 
 
+## Cameras
+
+The front color and infrared cameras have been tested with additional kernel and userspace changes. See [[Surface Laptop 1 camera support|Camera-Support#surface-laptop-1-cameras]] for dependencies, tested modes and current limitations.
+
 ## Thermal Throttling 
 That's right! Under prolonged  moderate to heavy load I found my pc thermal throttle on me (ceckertz155). In this article I will walk you through the steps experience to find out if you do too and what to do about it. First get ThermalMonitor and make sure your in the power group (you need to in order to use ThermalMonitor):
 `sudo gpasswd -a $USER power `
